    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Aga Khan University (AKU) is at the forefront of championing digital literacy in East Africa. This was demonstrated at its recent International Literacy Day celebration hosted by the University's Institute for Educational Development, East Africa (IED, EA) through its Centre for Education and Lifelong Learning (CELL) in Dar es Salaam. The event brought together educators, students, and academic leaders from across Tanzania to explore the evolving landscape of literacy in the digital age.",
